[AK - WHAT IS AEROPONICS] 
�
�
Aeroponics means growing plants without soil. Plant roots hang in air, and we spray them with water and
nutrients.
Normal farming needs soil, lots of water, lots of space, and you fight weeds and bugs. Aeroponics removes all
that. No soil = no weeds, no diseases, no pesticides. Food goes straight to roots.
[AK - HOW IT WORKS] 
�
�
Picture our tower. Inside, plant roots hang in a closed chamber – just hanging in air. Below is a water tank with
nutrients.
A pump sprays mist on the roots every few minutes. Plants take what they need. Extra water drips back into the
tank. Nothing wasted.
But we added something special – AI climate prediction. The system doesn't just spray on a timer. It predicts
upcoming weather and adjusts watering automatically. If it's going to be hot tomorrow, it waters more today.
This saves water and keeps plants healthy.
